id: pm-c6urop
title: Mixed linked-resource remove and add in one command silently favors removal
description: "The linked files/docs command accepts --remove and --add for the same path in one invocation, reports success, and leaves the path removed. Define and enforce an explicit conflict or atomic replace contract so evidence-maintenance intent cannot be silently lost."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 1
tags[6]: "area:cli","area:sdk",context-integrity,linked-resources,mutation-contract,ux
created_at: "2026-08-12T01:40:00.500Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-12T08:33:15.608Z"
assignee: "harness:codex"
claim_principal: "harness:codex#e92bb992d978060f83661c05"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: Same-path remove-plus-add has an explicit public contract; CLI and SDK apply the same contract to files and docs; zero partial history transitions are written; focused and manual regressions cover conflicting and non-conflicting compound mutations
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make compound linked-resource mutations deterministic and lossless
value: Agents can update evidence metadata without a successful command silently deleting the intended replacement
impact: Prevents context loss during file and doc link maintenance
outcome: Same-path remove-plus-add either atomically replaces the entry or fails with actionable guidance
why_now: Observed while correcting linked evidence for pm-cg1sjb during PR #983
parent: pm-doxj
risk: medium
confidence: high
reporter: "harness:codex"
severity: medium
environment: pm-cli 2026.8.11 built from PR #983 checkout
repro_steps: "Run pm files <id> --remove <path> --add path=<path>,scope=project,note=<new>; inspect pm get <id> and observe that the path is absent"
expected_result: The command preserves the added replacement or rejects the contradictory mutation before writing history
actual_result: The command succeeds but removal wins and the requested replacement is absent
affected_version: 2026.8.11
component: linked files/docs CLI and SDK mutation orchestration
regression: false
