comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-12T01:40:00.500Z","harness:codex","Duplicate-check evidence: searched all statuses for mixed remove/add, same-path linked-resource precedence, atomic replacement, and linked evidence repair. Closed pm-cstuys owns explicit replace-files/replace-docs but not the simultaneously accepted --remove plus --add ambiguity; related pm-cg1sjb is where the behavior was reproduced. This is new follow-up work and remains open/unclaimed."
  "2026-08-12T08:32:08.040Z","harness:codex","Implementation evidence: files/docs now normalize and anchor additions/removals, apply declared migrations, and reject every intersecting path before mutateItem or history append. The typed usage refusal is linked_artifact_mutation_conflict with same_path_added_and_removed context and deterministically sorted conflicts. The primitive is exported from @unbrained/pm-cli/sdk and recorded in generated error/runtime/public-surface contracts."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-12T08:32:08.487Z","harness:codex","Atomicity decision: a mixed add/remove batch is accepted only when the normalized post-migration sets are disjoint. Replacement remains possible as two separately messaged commands, making each immutable history event unambiguous."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-12T08:32:09.021Z","harness:codex","Package-boundary acceptance is essential for SDK work: source tests initially proved the primitive but the packed consumer exposed a missing top-level export. Repacking and importing @unbrained/pm-cli/sdk caught and closed that gap before PR creation."
